The point :-)

Nethack's encumbrance units, as in, well, every sanely designed P&P RPG
ever and even many of the not-so-sanely designed ones, are an abstract
index taking into account not only the item's weight but how cumbersome
it is to carry.  I've always regarded it as a great mistake to call an
encumbrance unit anything other than "a unit", though it may help
immersion to give some notes on the *typical* correspondence between
weight and encumbrance for sensibly-shaped objects.

YAI: Armour in your inventory or a carried container should have a
higher encumbrance value than armour on your body.  The easiest way
to carry a suit of armour, as long as it *fits* you, is to wear it.
This distributes the weight in a much more comfortable fashion than if
it's a lump of dead weight hanging from your back.)
